module dcr_load_ctor_dimension_silent

// D3 decompose-phase RED before-image for PRD `docs/prds/v0_6/dimension-checked-readers.md`
// leaves γ1 / γ2 / γ3 (boundary rows B1, B2, B3).
//
// All four load structures declare their magnitude field as `Real`
// (crates/reify-compiler/stdlib/fea_multi_case.ri PointLoad:317, PressureLoad:419,
// TractionLoad:448, BodyForce:478). MEASURED at decompose (2026-07-28,
// main efba5a8036):
//
//   * the units-CORRECT spelling `force: 5000N` emits only a WARNING
//     ("argument 'force' has type 'Scalar[m*kg*s^-2]' but param 'force'
//      requires type 'Real'") and stores a `Value::Scalar`;
//   * `extract_loads` (crates/reify-eval/src/compute_targets/elastic_static.rs:4029)
//     matches `Some(Value::Real(f))` ONLY, so that Scalar contributes ZERO force
//     to `solve_elastic_static`, while `extract_total_load`
//     (buckling.rs:726/:730) accepts both and contributes 5000 N;
//   * `TractionLoad` and `BodyForce` have ZERO occurrences anywhere in
//     elastic_static.rs (verified by grep at decompose) — they are dropped
//     silently (INV-SF-3);
//   * `reify eval` EXIT 0.
//
// At decompose this file EVALUATED CLEAN (exit 0), and the plan was for γ3 to
// make the bare spellings exit 1 with a coded Error, and TractionLoad/BodyForce
// reaching a solver exit 1 with `FeaLoadKindUnsupported`. Since δ (#5306) the
// file exits 1 BEFORE any γ leaf lands, on the ctor-conformance chokepoint
// recorded below. That exit 1 is NOT γ1's, γ2's or γ3's signal.
//
// POST-δ RE-MEASUREMENT (2026-09-25, main 12a9da343d; #5306 flipped
// CTOR_FIELD_CONFORMANCE_SEVERITY to Error):
//   `reify check` EXIT 1 / `reify eval` EXIT 1, two Errors:
//   * ArgTypeMismatch, PointLoad.force on `dimensioned_point`:
//     Scalar[m·kg·s^-2] at a field still declared `Real`;
//   * ArgTypeMismatch, TractionLoad.traction on `traction`:
//     Scalar[kg·m^-1·s^-2] at a field still declared `Real`.
//   The bare spellings raise nothing. CHOKEPOINT: compile-time struct-ctor field
//   conformance, so eval stops at compile. Machine pin: the gate-resident
//   `ctor_conformance_corpus_residual_entries_are_all_live` (reify-compiler,
//   harness_compilation_surface/ctor_conformance_corpus_survey.rs).
//
//   How each leaf reads its own signal now:
//   * γ2 (#6941) retypes the four fields, which makes its signal compile-time
//     and direct: both Errors above vanish, and the three bare spellings
//     (`bare_point`, `bare_pressure`, `body_force`) each raise ctor-conformance
//     ArgTypeMismatch instead. PREDICTION, probe-backed: a local
//     `param force : Force` twin given `force: 1000.0` measured the Error
//     "argument 'force' has type 'Real' but param 'force' requires type
//     'Scalar[m·kg·s^-2]'". So the file STILL exits 1 after γ2, on the opposite
//     bindings, and γ2 must read its signal from the per-binding diagnostic
//     set, never from the exit code. γ2's diff also deletes this file's `force`
//     and `traction` CTOR_CONFORMANCE_CORPUS_RESIDUAL entries.
//   * γ3 (#5802): its B2 row (bare spelling -> DimensionedArgRejected) is
//     pre-empted from `.ri`, because after γ2 a bare load never reaches
//     `extract_loads`. γ3 observes its reader narrowing below the compiler: a
//     Rust test hands the load reader a hand-built Value and asserts
//     `DiagnosticCode::DimensionedArgRejected` identity (INV-SF-6), the code
//     ruling esc-5791-3 names for reader rejections. Its B3 row
//     (`FeaLoadKindUnsupported`) needs a solver call, which this file never
//     makes.
//   * γ1 (#6922): see `dcr_solver_load_dropped_dimensioned.ri`.

structure def DcrLoadCtorDimensionSilent {
    let dimensioned_point = PointLoad(point: "tip", force: 5000N)
    let bare_point        = PointLoad(point: "tip", force: 5000.0)
    let bare_pressure     = PressureLoad(magnitude: 1000000.0)
    let traction          = TractionLoad(face: "top", traction: 5000000Pa)
    let body_force        = BodyForce(body: "all", force_density: -77000.0)
}
